detaileddescription.para:
Multistage Table Algorithm
The lookup uses a three-level table to compress the full Unicode range (U+0000 to U+10FFFF) into a compact representation. Given a codepoint cp: uint8_tt1_index=charPropsT1[cp>>CHAR_PROPS_SHIFT];
uint16_tt2_index=charPropsT2[(t1_index<<CHAR_PROPS_SHIFT)+(cp&CHAR_PROPS_MASK)];
autoprops=charPropsT3[t2_index];


Table dimensions:

charPropsT1: 4352 entries (uint8_t), indexed by cp >> 8

charPropsT2: 46592 entries (uint16_t), indexed by (T1 << 8) + (cp & 0xFF)

graphemeSegT3: 550 entries (uint16_t), final property values
